Third-party software redistributed with this package

@xynogen/pix-pretty — MIT — https://github.com/xynogen/pix-mono
  Draws the comparison shown in the review: gutter, line numbers, row tints,
  word-level emphasis and syntax colouring. Installed as a runtime dependency and
  therefore redistributed with this package, together with its own dependencies:
  @xynogen/pix-runtime (MIT), chalk (MIT), cli-highlight (MIT), diff (BSD-3-Clause)
  and @ff-labs/fff-node (MIT) with its platform binaries.

jiti — MIT — https://github.com/unjs/jiti
  Loads the TypeScript sources @xynogen/pix-pretty publishes. Node refuses to
  strip types from a file under node_modules, so the package asks for this loader
  itself rather than relying on the host to have registered one.
